From: grimtickle-overlay <overlay@grimtickle.local>
Date: Thu, 03 Jul 2026 07:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] systemd: Only start corosync if config file exists

Adds ConditionPathExists=/etc/corosync/corosync.conf to the corosync
service unit. Without this, systemd attempts to start corosync on boot
even on nodes that have not yet been added to a cluster (no conf file),
which causes a failed unit and noise in the journal.

On a freshly installed pxvirt node, /etc/corosync/corosync.conf does
not exist until 'pvecm create' or 'pvecm add' is run. This condition
prevents the spurious failure.

Originally from Fabian Grünbichler <f.gruenbichler@proxmox.com>.
Adapted for corosync 3.1.10 (service files moved to init/systemd/).

---
 init/systemd/corosync.service.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/init/systemd/corosync.service.in
+++ b/init/systemd/corosync.service.in
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 Description=Corosync Cluster Engine
 Documentation=man:corosync man:corosync.conf man:corosync_overview
 ConditionKernelCommandLine=!nocluster
+ConditionPathExists=/etc/corosync/corosync.conf
 Requires=network-online.target
 After=network-online.target

